Subject: [PATCH] cmake: allow static builds on Substrate

STATICDEVEL is gated to Linux only:

    if(STATICDEVEL AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
      message(FATAL_ERROR "Static builds are only supported on Linux.")

Substrate is an ELF platform on the same GNU toolchain, and its
Platform/Substrate CMake module defers to Platform/Linux for every
link/soname/rpath convention, so nothing about a static build differs
here.  Substrate names its platform honestly instead of pretending to be
Linux, so add it to the match.

Same change as the sdl2-compat port carries, for the same reason.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 option(SDL12DEVEL "Enable installing SDL-1.2 development headers" ON)
 option(STATICDEVEL "Enable installing static link library" OFF)
 
-if(STATICDEVEL AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
+if(STATICDEVEL AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux|Substrate"))
   message(FATAL_ERROR "Static builds are only supported on Linux.")
 endif()
 
